    <bpmn:process id="W_W4850" name="W4850. Multi-Site Permit Renewal Campaigns (LGU Business Permit, Mayor&#x27;s Permit, BFP FSIC)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual LGU business-permit renewal season (Jan); annual BFP FSIC; recurring multi-site cycles
Frequency: Annual per site (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ) for LGU; periodic for BFP
Volume: ~205 sites × LGU business permit/mayor&#x27;s permit annually; ~205 × BFP FSIC
Owner: Compliance Operations / Store Ops (VS-07) / LGU Compliance (VS-76)
Participants: Store Managers, DC Managers, Real Estate (VS-97), Finance (VS-17 fees), Third-party providers (W4854)
Source: workflow W4850 — Multi-Site Permit Renewal Campaigns (LGU Business Permit, Mayor&#x27;s Permit, BFP FSIC)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4850_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4850_Lane1" name="Compliance Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4850_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4850_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4850_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4850_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4850_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4850_Start3" name="Annual LGU business-permit renewal season (Jan); annual BFP FSIC; recurring multi-site…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4850_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4850_Task4" name="Plan the annual campaign: the ~205-site LGU business-permit/mayor&#x27;s-permit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Plan the annual campaign: the ~205-site LGU business-permit/mayor&#x27;s-permit renewal schedule by LGU (different LGU deadlines &amp; requirements), the BFP FSIC cycle, owners per site (Store/DC Manager + central support), the standard package, fee budget, and the third-party-provider coverage (W4854); sequence by LGU deadline
Responsible (R): Compliance Operations / Store Ops / LGU Compliance
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Campaign planning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4850_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4850_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4850_Task5" name="Execute the campaign across sites: distribute packages to Store/DC Managers (or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Execute the campaign across sites: distribute packages to Store/DC Managers (or providers), track submission per site, manage LGU-specific variations (barangay clearance, sanitation, fire-safety eval), collect renewed permits, and reconcile to the calendar (W4845) and register (W4842)
Responsible (R): Compliance Operations / Store Managers / Providers
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Campaign window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4850_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4850_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4850_Task6" name="Close the campaign: confirm 100% coverage, remediate any lapses (W4853), report…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Close the campaign: confirm 100% coverage, remediate any lapses (W4853), report campaign results (on-time %, lapses, cost) to governance (W4864), and capture LGU-process learnings for next year
Responsible (R): Compliance Operations / Analytics
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Post-campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4850_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4850_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4850_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4850_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-729 (ensure controlled execution — Renewal Execution, Inspection Coordination &amp; Multi-Site Campaigns (PA-166.2).) | - CTL-729: 100% site coverage targeted; per-LGU deadlines tracked; lapses remediated; campaign results reported
Owner: Compliance Operations / Store Ops (VS-07) / LGU Compliance (VS-76)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4850_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4850_Annotation8" targetRef="W4850_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4850_Flow10" sourceRef="W4850_Start3" targetRef="W4850_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4850_Flow11" sourceRef="W4850_Task4" targetRef="W4850_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4850_Flow12" sourceRef="W4850_Task5" targetRef="W4850_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4850_Flow13" sourceRef="W4850_Task6" targetRef="W4850_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
