    <bpmn:process id="W_W4855" name="W4855. Inter-Agency Coordination &amp; Multi-Permit Concurrent Renewals" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Permits requiring multi-regulator sign-off (e.g., new store needs LGU + BFP + DENR + BIR); concurrent renewal cycles; conflicting regulator requirements
Frequency: Per multi-permit need
Volume: ~10–15 multi-permit acquisitions per year (one per new store) plus renewal campaigns
Owner: Compliance Operations / Regulatory Intelligence (W4843)
Participants: Domain owners, Government Affairs (VS-104), Real Estate (VS-97), Legal (VS-100.3)
Source: workflow W4855 — Inter-Agency Coordination &amp; Multi-Permit Concurrent Renewals</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4855_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4855_Lane1" name="Regulatory Intelligence">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4855_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4855_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4855_Lane2" name="Compliance Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4855_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4855_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4855_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4855_Start4" name="Permits requiring multi-regulator sign-off (e.g., new store needs LGU + BFP + DENR +…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4855_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4855_Task5" name="Map the multi-permit dependency graph for the need (e.g., a new store: SEC/DTI…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Map the multi-permit dependency graph for the need (e.g., a new store: SEC/DTI → LGU business permit needs BFP FSIC + barangay clearance + DENR ECC + sanitary; BIR branch needs LGU permit); identify the critical path and sequencing constraints
Responsible (R): Regulatory Intelligence / Compliance Operations
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Per need</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4855_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4855_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4855_Task6" name="Coordinate concurrent renewals/acquisitions across regulators: sequence…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Coordinate concurrent renewals/acquisitions across regulators: sequence filings, manage cross-regulator dependencies (permit B needs permit A), resolve conflicting requirements, and leverage Government Affairs (VS-104) relationships to smooth bottlenecks
Responsible (R): Compliance Operations / Domain Owners / Government Affairs
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Per need</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4855_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4855_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4855_Task7" name="Track the multi-permit bundle to completion, update the register (W4842), and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Track the multi-permit bundle to completion, update the register (W4842), and capture inter-agency-process learnings (e.g., a region where DENR-BFP sequencing is slow) for the obligation map (W4843) and analytics (W4862)
Responsible (R): Compliance Operations / Regulatory Intelligence
Accountable (A): Compliance Portfolio Manager
Duration: Per need</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4855_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4855_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4855_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4855_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-729 (ensure controlled execution — Renewal Execution, Inspection Coordination &amp; Multi-Site Campaigns (PA-166.2).) | - CTL-729: dependency graph followed; conflicts escalated via Government Affairs/Legal; bundle tracked to completion
Owner: Compliance Operations / Regulatory Intelligence (W4843)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
